&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking a Data Projects Intern to join our Data Projects team in Edinburgh for Summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being a part of the AddeU Internship Program, you will be working on meaningful project(s) that you can feel proud of and present back to the company at the end of the experience. In addition to having a supporting manager and mentor, we have a fantastic onboarding program to get you acclimated and ready for your time with us. Fun events and super cool swag are also included!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Data Projects Intern, you will split time between executing on the team&#39;s existing backlog of data feed and reconciliation work (~80%) and building lightweight automation tooling (~20%). The Data Projects team owns pipelines for the ingestion of client data and the reconciliation workflows that underpin every client engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based full-time in our Edinburgh office and requires in-person attendance for the duration of the internship. Dates are currently set for June - August 2027 but please advise your recruiter if you have any timing constraints. Relocation assistance is not offered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis between November 2026 and March 2027. We encourage you to apply early, as we may close the posting once the program is filled.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete scoped feed and reconciliation tasks from the team&#39;s backlogs including new historical feed builds, transaction/security type mapping, data validation, and support for Enterprise client onboarding/conversion workflows (~80%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As appropriate help to build or extend Databricks apps, dashboards, and Claude Code skills following established team patterns (~20%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, document and design new workflows or improvements to existing data workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate repetitive steps in feed onboarding or data validation processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with senior analysts and participate in team planning and reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to measurable reduction in analyst hours for targeted workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a university or other post-secondary program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Mathematics, Finance, or a related field (penultimate or final year ideal, though all years are welcome to apply)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to commit to the full 12-week program, June 7th, 2027 - August 27th, 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data platforms such as Databricks, or willingness to learn quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail when working with data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with an ability to work independently on well-scoped tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
